course: dictionary
lesson: 9876
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around the word. Are there drawing boards, boats, horses, or plans nearby? Those clues point to the meaning.
explain: «Kieran's egg is stuck to the spoon with Blu Tack.» Stuck tells you the stuff holds things together, so it is a sticky fixing, not a sail or a saddle. Context works even when you do not know the brand.
explain: «Try a different tack» means try another way of doing something. Swap in the meaning of "way or plan" and check that the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Tack has several meanings: a small nail, to fix or sew something loosely, a way of doing something, and the equipment for riding a horse.
fact: To tack a boat is to turn its front through the wind, so it can zigzag against the wind.
fact: «Tacked on» means added at the end, often as an afterthought, as in «"like" is tacked on the end of a question».
exercise: «Mia used a tack to pin her drawing to the noticeboard.» What is a tack here? | Horse equipment | A kind of cloth | A sailing plan | *A small nail with a flat head
exercise: «The sailing boat had to tack to get past the wind.» What does tack mean? | Ride a horse | Stop dead in the water | Sew with big loose stitches | *Zigzag against the wind by turning its front through it
exercise: «When the first plan failed, Sam decided to try a different tack.» What does tack mean? | *A way or plan of doing something | A small nail | A horse's saddle | A sailing boat
test: «Before the party, Dad tacked the banner to the wall.» What does tacked mean? | Ate it | Painted it | *Fixed it with tacks | Folded it neatly
test: «At the stables, Ella cleaned the tack before her ride.» What is tack here? | A sticky putty | A small nail | *Saddle, bridle and other riding equipment | A sailing plan
exam: In «"like" is tacked on the end of a question», what does tacked on mean? | Steered a boat through the wind | Pinned to a board | Sewn very tightly | *Added at the end, often as an afterthought
